          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Running Telegram with a C script typically involves using the Telegram Bot API or interacting with the Telegram CLI client. Here are the possible approaches:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Using Telegram CLI (td-cli)**\nTelegram provides a command-line interface called [`td-cli`](https://github.com/tdlib/td) (based on TDLib). You can interact with it using a C script.\n\n#### **Steps:**\n1. **Install td-cli**\n   - On Linux:\n     ```sh\n     sudo apt install telegram-cli\n     ```\n   - On macOS:\n     ```sh\n     brew install telegram-cli\n     ```\n   - On Windows: Use [Cygwin](https://www.cygwin.com/) or WSL.\n\n2. **Run the Telegram CLI**\n   ```sh\n   telegram-cli -k tg-server.pub\n   ```\n\n3. **Control Telegram using C**\n   - Use `popen()` in C to execute Telegram CLI commands.\n\n   ```c\n   #include <stdio.h>\n   #include <stdlib.h>\n\n   int main() {\n       FILE *fp;\n       char command[] = \"telegram-cli -W -e 'msg @username Hello from C!'\";\n\n       // Execute Telegram CLI command\n       fp = popen(command, \"r\");\n       if (fp == NULL) {\n           printf(\"Failed to run Telegram CLI\\n\");\n           return 1;\n       }\n\n       // Close the process\n       pclose(fp);\n       return 0;\n   }\n   ```\n   This sends a message to `@username` from the C program.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Using Telegram Bot API with C**\nIf you are working with a Telegram bot, you can use the Telegram Bot"
