        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To run Telegram with a C script in **Termux** (Android terminal emulator), you have a few options:  \n\n---\n\n## **1. Using Telegram CLI (`tg-cli`)**  \nYou can use `telegram-cli` to send messages from your C program.  \n\n### **Step 1: Install Telegram CLI in Termux**  \n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade\npkg install git curl jq\ngit clone --recursive https://github.com/vysheng/tg.git && cd tg\npkg install libjansson-dev libconfig-dev libreadline-dev liblua-dev\npkg install libevent-dev openssl-tool make clang\n./configure\nmake\n```\n\n### **Step 2: Run Telegram CLI**\n```sh\nbin/telegram-cli -k tg-server.pub\n```\nThis will prompt you to enter your Telegram phone number for authentication.\n\n---\n\n## **2. Send Messages Using C and Telegram CLI**  \nOnce `telegram-cli` is set up, you can call it from a C program.\n\n### **Example C Code**  \n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint main() {\n    FILE *fp;\n    char command[] = \"bin/telegram-cli -W -e 'msg @username Hello from Termux C script!'\";\n\n    // Execute Telegram CLI command\n    fp = popen(command, \"r\");\n    if (fp == NULL) {\n        printf(\"Failed to send message\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    // Close the process\n    pclose(fp);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n### **Step 3: Compile and Run the C Script**\n```sh\nclang telegram.c -o telegram\n./telegram\n```\n\n---\n\n## **3. Using Telegram Bot API in C**  \nIf you want to send messages using a bot instead, use Telegram’s Bot API.  \nYou need a **bot token** (from [BotFather](https://t.me/BotFather)) and a **chat ID**.\n\n### **Example C Code for Bot API**  \n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint main() {\n    char command[512];\n    char *bot_token = \"YOUR_BOT_TOKEN\";\n    char *chat_id = \"YOUR_CHAT_ID\";\n    char *message = \"Hello from C in Termux!\";\n\n    snprintf(command, sizeof(command),\n             \"curl -s -X POST https://api.telegram.org/bot%s/sendMessage -d chat_id=%s -d text=\\\"%s\\\"\",\n             bot_token, chat_id, message);\n\n    system(command);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n### **Step 3: Compile and Run**\n```sh\nclang bot.c -o bot\n./bot\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Which One to Use?**  \n- **If you want to control your personal Telegram account** → Use **Telegram CLI**  \n- **If you want to automate messaging** → Use **Telegram Bot API**  \n\nLet me know if you need more help setting it up!"
          ]
