        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To remove all JSON lock files in Termux, follow these steps:\n\n### **1. Remove All `.json` and `.lock` Files**  \nRun this command in Termux:  \n```sh\nrm -f *.json *.lock\n```\nThis will delete all JSON and lock files in the current directory.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Remove JSON Lock Files Recursively (All Directories)**\nIf you want to delete JSON lock files across all subdirectories, use:  \n```sh\nfind . -type f \\( -name \"*.json\" -o -name \"*.lock\" \\) -delete\n```\nThis command searches for `.json` and `.lock` files in all folders and removes them.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Confirm Deleted Files**\nAfter running the command, check if the files are removed:  \n```sh\nls -al | grep -E '\\.json|\\.lock'\n```\nIf nothing appears, the files are deleted.\n\nLet me know if you need further help!"
