        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To create a brand new Python project in **Termux**, follow these steps:  \n\n---\n\n## **1. Install Python (if not installed)**\n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade\npkg install python -y\n```\n\n---\n\n## **2. Create a New Project Directory**\nNavigate to a location where you want to create the project, then create a new folder:  \n```sh\nmkdir my_python_project && cd my_python_project\n```\n\n---\n\n## **3. Set Up a Virtual Environment (Optional)**\nA virtual environment helps manage dependencies:  \n```sh\npython -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\n```\nIf `venv` is not installed, install it:  \n```sh\npkg install python-venv -y\n```\n\n---\n\n## **4. Create a Main Python File**\n```sh\ntouch main.py\necho 'print(\"Hello, Termux Python Project!\")' > main.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## **5. Install Project Dependencies (if needed)**\nExample: Install Flask  \n```sh\npip install flask\n```\nTo save dependencies:  \n```sh\npip freeze > requirements.txt\n```\nTo install them later:  \n```sh\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n## **6. Run Your Python Script**\n```sh\npython main.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## **7. (Optional) Initialize Git for Version Control**\n```sh\npkg install git -y\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit\"\n```\n\nNow you have a fully set up Python project in Termux! Let me know if you need help."
          ]
