        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Since you're using **Termux on Android**, here’s how to properly set up a **new Python project** in Termux.  \n\n---\n\n### **1. Install Python in Termux**  \nFirst, update and install Python:  \n```sh\npkg update && pkg upgrade -y\npkg install python -y\n```\nCheck if Python is installed:  \n```sh\npython --version\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. Create a New Project Folder**  \nNavigate to your preferred location and create a project directory:  \n```sh\nmkdir my_python_project && cd my_python_project\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. Set Up a Virtual Environment (Optional but Recommended)**  \nA virtual environment helps manage dependencies separately.  \n```sh\npkg install python-venv -y\npython -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\n```\nNow, your project is using an isolated Python environment.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Create a Python Script**  \n```sh\ntouch main.py\necho 'print(\"Hello from Termux Python Project!\")' > main.py\n```\nTo edit the script, use a text editor:  \n```sh\nnano main.py\n```\nWrite your Python code, save it (`CTRL + X`, then `Y`, then `Enter`).\n\n---\n\n### **5. Install Dependencies (If Needed)**  \nFor example, install Flask:  \n```sh\npip install flask\n```\nTo save installed dependencies:  \n```sh\npip freeze > requirements.txt\n```\nTo install dependencies later:  \n```sh\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n### **6. Run the Python Script**  \n```sh\npython main.py\n```\n\n---\n\n### **7. (Optional) Initialize Git for Version Control**  \nIf you plan to use Git:  \n```sh\npkg install git -y\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit\"\n```\n\n---\n\nNow you have a brand-new Python project **ready to go** in Termux! Let me know if you need more help."
          ]
        },
