        "create_time": 1738532890.445462,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "In **Termux**, you can find your project directory using the following methods:  \n\n---\n\n### **1. Check Current Directory**  \nIf you are inside your project folder, run:  \n```sh\npwd\n```\nThis will print the full path of your current directory.  \n\n---\n\n### **2. List Files and Folders**  \nTo see all files and directories inside Termux:  \n```sh\nls\n```\nIf your project is in the **home** directory, list all files there:  \n```sh\nls ~/  \n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. Find Your Project Folder**  \nIf you don’t remember where your project is, search for it:  \n```sh\nfind ~ -type d -name \"my_python_project\"\n```\nReplace `\"my_python_project\"` with your actual project folder name.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Change to Your Project Directory**  \nIf your project is in `~/my_python_project`, navigate to it:  \n```sh\ncd ~/my_python_project\n```\nThen confirm you’re in the right place:  \n```sh\npwd\nls\n```\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you need more help!"
          ]
        },
